course: dictionary
lesson: 3720
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer wants. The word flight is a good example. «Our flight to Dublin leaves at nine» means a trip in an aeroplane. «Birds in flight» means flying through the air.
explain: Look at the words around the word. If the sentence mentions tickets, planes or airports, flight means a trip by air. If it mentions steps and floors, flight means a set of stairs, like «2 flights of stairs» from floor 1 to floor 3.
explain: Context can also show a meaning you may not expect. «Take flight» means running away from danger, so an animal that takes flight is leaving in a hurry because it is scared. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: Flight means a trip in an aeroplane, such as «our flight to Dublin».
fact: Flight also means the act of flying through the air, as in «birds in flight».
fact: A flight of stairs is a set of steps between two floors.
fact: «Take flight» means running away from danger.
fact: «Flight» can be a noun for a trip, a movement through the air, or a set of stairs, so check the context.
exercise: «Our flight to Dublin leaves at nine o'clock.» What does flight mean here? | Running away from danger | *A trip in an aeroplane | A set of steps between two floors | Feathers on a bird
exercise: «Navigators read the stars, the waves and the flight of birds.» What does flight mean here? | A flight of stairs | Running away from danger | *Flying through the air | A trip in a boat
exercise: «The animals took flight when the fire started.» What does took flight mean? | Stayed very still and quiet | Asked the farmer for help | Lay down to sleep | *Ran away from danger
test: «Going from floor 1 to floor 6 is 5 flights.» What is a flight in this sentence? | The act of flying through the air | Running away from danger | *A set of steps between two floors | A trip in an aeroplane
test: «Owls have soft fringed feathers that make their flight silent.» What does flight mean here? | A trip by plane | A flight of stairs | *The act of flying through the air | Running away from danger
exam: «Her flight was delayed, so we waited at the airport.» What does flight mean here? | Running away from danger | A set of steps between floors | Feathers on a wing | *A trip by aeroplane
